\image{conf-hanein-dry-electrodes.jpg}

\p{\strong{Caption.} Soft, screen-printed \strong{dry carbon electrode arrays} for simultaneous transcutaneous electrical stimulation and biopotential recording — a wearable, gel-free path toward closed-loop neuromodulation. Demonstrations span facial neuromodulation (EMG-triggered), \strong{transorbital stimulation evoking phosphenes} (a directly-induced visual quale), transcutaneous vagus nerve stimulation, and sleep. Activation/discomfort thresholds were comparable to wet gel electrodes.}
